I just did something I thought was mildly clever with a 
level 11ish lawful caveman who so far (down to lvl 27/ Medusa) 
hasn't found a single altar not watched over by a cross-aligned
priest:

1. Bought some protection in Minetown.

2. Converted the altar through sacrifice, and used a wand
to teleport the priest out of the temple.

3. Realized that I'm not all that comfortable with the
priest wandering around. 

3. With sudden inspiration, I got the priest to follow me into
another room in Minetown. I locked the room from the inside,
and teleported myself out.

Viola. Neutralized priest (at least until someone digs him out), 
and no murder charge. 



Actually, it turned out to be a much more dangerous plan
than I'd realized at first: in the time it was taking to
try to lock the door with a pick, the priest very nearly killed 
me. Twice. (Burned two potions of full healing.) I finally
understood that I wasn't just getting unlucky--I'd never be
able to lock the door in time-- and put him to sleep. 

I wouldn't try it again without some sort of magical locking
available.



(Postscript: Not 5 minutes later, I sacrificed a dward lord
on the altar, having completley forgotten that I was playing
a dwarf, and the hole effort was completely shot.)


